// A diagnostic about a line break points at the line break.
//
// The statement-boundary token was stamped wherever the *next* real token
// began, because `skipTrivia` consumed the break and then every blank line,
// comment and unit of indentation after it, and only then was the position
// read. So "found a line break" pointed at the line *below* the break and
// underlined the next arm — every other position in the file was right, which
// made the wrong one harder to disbelieve.
//
// Here the missing `=>` belongs at the end of the arm `1`, and that is where
// the caret goes.
let x = match 1 {
  1
  _ => 2,
}
print(x)
